# Zustand Store Patterns

- Keep stores focused on shared client state and state transitions. Put API requests, routing, and heavy data shaping in hooks or `src/services/` / `src/lib/`.
- Define an explicit state interface and typed action signatures for every store.
- Prefer immutable `set` updates and small action methods over one large catch-all updater.
- Derive or compute values in selectors/helpers when possible instead of storing duplicated data.
- When a store grows complex, extract pure helpers to `src/lib/` and keep the store responsible for orchestration only.

```ts
interface WorkspaceState {
  workspaceId: number | null;
  setWorkspaceId: (workspaceId: number | null) => void;
}
```

```ts
// Prefer focused actions
setWorkspaceId: (workspaceId) => set({ workspaceId })
```
